<custom_item>
  type              : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
  description       : "1.0415 - MSSRV - Ensure Enable Structured Exception Handling Overwrite Protection (SEHOP) is set to Enabled"
  info              : "Windows includes support for Structured Exception Handling Overwrite Protection (SEHOP)."
  solution          : "To establish the recommended configuration via GP, set the following UI path to Enabled : Computer Configuration\Policies\Administrative Templates\MS Security Guide\Enable Structured Exception Handling Overwrite Protection (SEHOP) Note: This Group Policy path does not exist by default. An additional Group Policy template ( SecGuide.admx/adml ) is required - it is available from Microsoft at this link https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/download/details.aspx?id=55319. More information is available at MSKB 956607: How to enable Structured Exception Handling Overwrite Protection (SEHOP) in Windows operating systems https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/help/956607/how-to-enable-structured-exception-handling-overwrite-protection-sehop Impact: After you enable SEHOP, existing versions of Cygwin, Skype, and Armadillo-protected applications may not work correctly."
  reference         : "NIST 800-53r5|SI-16"
  see_also          : "See HTH Policies and Standards"
  value_type        : POLICY_TEXT
  value_data        : "0"
  powershell_option : CAN_BE_NULL
  powershell_args   : "-NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Command '-NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Command ''$__pysc_result = (& { (Get-ItemProperty -Path ''''HKLM:\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session Manager\kernel'''' -Name ''''DisableExceptionChainValidation'''' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).DisableExceptionChainValidation } | Out-String); if([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace([string]$__pysc_result)){ Write-Output ''''__NON_COMPLIANT__'''' } else { Write-Output ($__pysc_result.Trim()) }'''"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type              : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
  description       : "1.0416 - MSSRV - Ensure NetBT NodeType configuration is set to Enabled: P-node (recommended)"
  info              : "This setting determines which method NetBIOS over TCP/IP (NetBT) uses to register and resolve names."
  solution          : "To establish the recommended configuration via GP, set the following UI path to Enabled: P-node (recommended) : Computer Configuration\Policies\Administrative Templates\MS Security Guide\NetBT NodeType configuration Note: This change does not take effect until the computer has been restarted. Note #2: This Group Policy path does not exist by default. An additional Group Policy template ( SecGuide.admx/adml ) is required - it is available from Microsoft at this link https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/download/details.aspx?id=55319 . Please note that this setting is only available in the Security baseline (FINAL) for Windows 10 v1903 and Windows Server v1903 (or newer) release of SecGuide.admx/adml, so if you previously downloaded this template, you may need to update it from a newer Microsoft baseline to get this new NetBT NodeType configuration setting. Impact: NetBIOS name resolution queries will require a defined and available WINS server for external NetBIOS name resolution. If a WINS server is not defined or not reachable, and the desired hostname is not defined in the local cache, local LMHOSTS or HOSTS files, NetBIOS name resolution will fail."
  reference         : "NIST 800-53r5|CM-1 CM-2 CM-6 CM-7 CM-7(1) CM-9 SA-3 SA-8 SA-10"
  see_also          : "See HTH Policies and Standards"
  value_type        : POLICY_TEXT
  value_data        : "2"
  powershell_option : CAN_BE_NULL
  powershell_args   : "-NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Command '-NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Command ''$__pysc_result = (& { (Get-ItemProperty -Path ''''HKLM:\System\CurrentControlSet\Services\NetBT\Parameters'''' -Name ''''NodeType'''' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).NodeType } | Out-String); if([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace([string]$__pysc_result)){ Write-Output ''''__NON_COMPLIANT__'''' } else { Write-Output ($__pysc_result.Trim()) }'''"
</custom_item>

